title: mf slow list
tags: [[CLI command]] [[Slow log]]
kind: reference
summary: List the slow operations, newest first — the default

The newest entries first, both processes merged: [[Diagnosing a slow operation]].
Times are in the local time zone (`TZ`, else the system's); `--json` keeps the
logged Unix milliseconds (`at_ms`), which `mf slow replay --at` takes.
`--since` takes the durations of `mf trash prune -d` (`30m`, `2h`, `7d`), `--min`
the same durations for the entries that took at least that long (`mf slow --min 60s`:
only what took a minute, however far back — the daemon filters before `--limit`
cuts), `--op` keeps the entries whose operation contains a substring, `--json`
prints the raw entries one per line.
